WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.510 --> 00:00:03.639
Speaker 1: Hey, this is really interesting
news out of Texas.

00:00:03.639 --> 00:00:09.340
Actor Matthew McConaughey or McConaughey,
as some people like to say, is polling 12

00:00:09.340 --> 00:00:13.280
points ahead of Republican Texas Governor
Greg Abbott.

00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:14.690
He's not running.

00:00:14.690 --> 00:00:19.390
If your reaction was I didn't know that he
was running, he's not.

00:00:19.390 --> 00:00:25.010
This is a new poll from the Dallas Morning
News and the University of Texas, Tyler.

00:00:25.010 --> 00:00:33.589
It's based on 1100 registered voters, 30 percent
Democrats, 37 percent Republicans, 33 percent

00:00:33.589 --> 00:00:39.960
who are neither 45 percent of voters say they
would support Matthew McConaughey over Greg

00:00:39.960 --> 00:00:43.319
Abbott if Matthew McConaughey were to run
for governor.

00:00:43.319 --> 00:00:48.379
33 percent said they'd support Abbott over
McConaghy, 22 percent say they would vote

00:00:48.379 --> 00:00:51.429
for someone else or aren't really sure.

00:00:51.429 --> 00:00:56.390
This is interesting because McConaghy has
actually kind of teased and alluded to maybe

00:00:56.390 --> 00:00:59.369
running in the state of Texas.

00:00:59.369 --> 00:01:01.219
He is not confirmed.

00:01:01.219 --> 00:01:04.629
He told CNBC last month he is not joking.

00:01:04.629 --> 00:01:07.340
He said, quote, I'm not teasing the idea.

00:01:07.340 --> 00:01:11.360
I'm actually looking at the idea and giving
it serious consideration.

00:01:11.360 --> 00:01:14.230
I have a new chapter for myself personally
in my life.

00:01:14.230 --> 00:01:15.990
I believe it's some sort of leadership role.

00:01:15.990 --> 00:01:17.090
I don't know what the role is.

00:01:17.090 --> 00:01:18.610
I don't know my category.

00:01:18.610 --> 00:01:24.380
We've been talking about the why of leadership
and even I would say we need some more good

00:01:24.380 --> 00:01:25.870
leaders.

00:01:25.870 --> 00:01:28.270
This would be fascinating.

00:01:28.270 --> 00:01:30.280
So there's two parts to this.

00:01:30.280 --> 00:01:35.040
I don't know how much this says about Matthew
McConaughey specifically.

00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:40.410
What I mean by that is Greg Abbott has so
mismanaged almost everything.

00:01:40.410 --> 00:01:47.120
I mean, the pandemic, the power outage and
grid, the electrical grid situation, he's

00:01:47.120 --> 00:01:50.810
a complete and total clown who doesn't seem
to care much about the health or safety or

00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:53.230
welfare of people in Texas.

00:01:53.230 --> 00:01:58.630
It's possible a random school teacher with
no name recognition would maybe do OK against

00:01:58.630 --> 00:01:59.630
Greg Abbott.

00:01:59.630 --> 00:02:02.229
So part of it is we have to figure out how
much of it is Matthew Matthew McConaughey

00:02:02.229 --> 00:02:04.310
specifically.

00:02:04.310 --> 00:02:08.380
But then you add in the fact that if you look
at Matthew McConaughey over the last 12 to

00:02:08.380 --> 00:02:12.010
18 months, I've been seeing him doing more
and more conversations and interviews with

00:02:12.010 --> 00:02:13.769
people in the political space.

00:02:13.769 --> 00:02:15.099
He does actually seem interested.

00:02:15.099 --> 00:02:16.510
He seems to be taking this seriously.

00:02:16.510 --> 00:02:17.629
I don't know the guy's politics.

00:02:17.629 --> 00:02:21.409
I have no idea whether he's a Democrat or
a Republican.

00:02:21.409 --> 00:02:22.530
I don't know anything about him.

00:02:22.530 --> 00:02:26.109
What I do know, though, is that.

00:02:26.109 --> 00:02:31.389
He at least doesn't seem like a radical right
winger if he is a centrist or further left,

00:02:31.389 --> 00:02:36.659
and if without even announcing a candidacy,
he is doing this well in Texas, what we saw

00:02:36.659 --> 00:02:44.010
in twenty twenty in Texas, the tightening
in Texas for Trump in his reelection campaign,

00:02:44.010 --> 00:02:47.620
which ultimately didn't end up being that
close, but it was could it could have been

00:02:47.620 --> 00:02:51.030
a much, much bigger margin for Donald Trump.

00:02:51.030 --> 00:02:54.510
This could signal significant changes in the
state of Texas.

00:02:54.510 --> 00:02:57.189
And we are all we can do is continue to follow
it.

00:02:57.189 --> 00:02:58.629
We've been talking about it before.

00:02:58.629 --> 00:03:02.469
Georgia and Texas have been the ones that
we've been watching relatively closely.

00:03:02.469 --> 00:03:03.469
Very interesting.

00:03:03.469 --> 00:03:04.760
And we're going to keep a close eye on that.

